@* EVT-3 Ticket 2 (owner verbatim, EVENT-ACCOUNTS-1: "events are keys that
   map to sets of Biblical accounts"; chronological traversal returns a SET
   of passage refs per hop, cardinality 1 valid): ONE reusable component for
   rendering a SET of passage refs with NO verse contents -- explorable
   (click pushes the ref's own node), reusable anywhere a set of passage
   refs renders (the owner's own composability bar: "make sure all the new
   bits made for this are composable and reusable").

   Retires ArrowNav.razor's own former EV-1 "always-visible primary-witness-
   verse line" (ref + first-verse REAL TEXT) -- the owner's later, more
   specific ruling on the SAME surface (UX-2 feedback, 2026-09-06, verbatim:
   "it does not appear to me that you did what i told you for the
   chronological thing (not showing the verse contents, just the list of
   refs)") supersedes EV-1's own "see the actual event-mapped verse" -- see
   ArrowNav.razor's own header comment for the fuller retirement story.

   Consumes DESCRIPTORS (<see cref="RefDescriptor"/>) rather than raw ref
   strings so callers stay fully in charge of what a ref's own click target
   actually is -- a VerseNode for a lone verse, a PassageNode for a genuine
   multi-verse span with its own already-known text (PassageList.Explore's
   own VerseNode/PassageNode identity choice, just pre-decided by the
   caller here instead of re-derived, since THIS component fetches/holds no
   verse text at all to re-derive it from). One-line knob: TestIdPrefix is
   the ONE parameter that changes which surface's own testid grammar a
   given RefsList instance uses. *@
@using BibleAtlas.Client.Explore

@if (Refs.Count > 0)
{
    <div class="popover-refs-list" data-testid="@TestIdPrefix">
        @foreach (var d in Refs)
        {
            <button type="button" class="popover-refs-list-item explorable" data-testid="@($"{TestIdPrefix}-{d.TestIdSuffix ?? d.Ref}")"
                    @onclick="@(() => OnExplore.InvokeAsync(d.Target))">@d.Ref</button>
        }
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// One explorable ref -- the display text (a span like "MAT.9.27-34" or
    /// a bare "MAT.9.27") paired with the node it opens. The caller decides
    /// the target's own identity (VerseNode vs. PassageNode) -- this
    /// component never re-derives it from the ref string alone.
    /// Batch ATTEST-1: <paramref name="TestIdSuffix"/> defaults to
    /// <paramref name="Ref"/>, so every pre-existing caller is unchanged
    /// byte-for-byte. It exists because ATTEST-1's own "SIMILAR ACCOUNTS"
    /// rows display an event TITLE ("A leper healed; great popular
    /// excitement") -- fine to read, a poor testid, and one that would
    /// churn every time a curator improves a label. Those rows pass the
    /// stable event id instead.
    public sealed record RefDescriptor(string Ref, IExplorable Target, string? TestIdSuffix = null);

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<RefDescriptor> Refs { get; set; } = Array.Empty<RefDescriptor>();
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string TestIdPrefix { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback<IExplorable> OnExplore { get; set; }
}
